  "name": "Generate Sora 2 videos and auto post to TikTok, Instagram Reels and YouTube Shorts",
  "tags": [],
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "39cebc27-7984-4280-aede-cf67d6315b0e",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -629,
        -97
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 520,
        "height": 812,
        "content": "## Generate Sora 2 videos from a list of ideas and post them\nTurn video ideas from Google Sheets into Sora 2 clips: every day OpenAI writes the prompt, Sora 2 renders a vertical clip and PostWire posts it to TikTok, Instagram Reels and YouTube Shorts with a caption for each network.\n\n### How it works\n1. **Every day at 9:00** reads the rows marked ready. **Take the next idea** picks the first one and **Mark the idea as generating** claims it, so a clip is never paid for twice.\n2. **Write the Sora 2 prompt** (OpenAI) returns the shot description, a caption idea and the YouTube title.\n3. **Sora 2 render** generates the clip in 9:16 and waits until it is ready.\n4. **Post to TikTok, Reels and Shorts** (PostWire) uploads the file, writes a caption per network and publishes.\n5. **Mark the idea as posted** writes the post links in the row. When Sora or a network refuses, **Write the fix in the row** and **Email me the fix** tell you what to fix.\n\n### Setup\n1. Install the verified **PostWire** node (search \"PostWire\" in the nodes panel), create an account at postwire.io, connect your networks and paste your API key into a **PostWire API** credential.\n2. Add an OpenAI credential to both OpenAI nodes. Sora 2 is billed per second of video (about 0.10 USD per second).\n3. Create a sheet with the columns idea, style, status, posted_at, links and note. Write ready in status to queue an idea, and pick the sheet in the four Sheets nodes.\n4. Connect Gmail and fill in **Channel settings**.\n\n### Customize\nChange the length (4, 8 or 12 seconds) or the style in Channel settings, or the networks in the PostWire node (the free plan posts to 2 networks per post)."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
